  "question": {
    "text": "A block is sliding down on an inclined plane of slope $\\theta$ and at an instant $t=0$ this block is given an upward momentum so that it starts moving up on the inclined surface with velocity $u$. The distance $(S)$ travelled by the block before its velocity become zero, is $\\_\\_\\_\\_$. <br> ($g=$ gravitational acceleration)",
